The road where reality ends


09 Dec 2020 14:34






Seeking Greenlights:  Yes

Page Type:  SCP article

Elevator Pitch:  A road extending out of a small town. No one knows where it leads to. Anyone who treads it disappears from sight after passing a certain point, their dead body reappearing some days later, the cause of death usually being either suicide or dehydration/starvation. Attempts to use any type of electronic device for communication with test subjects/surveillance has failed.

Central Narrative:  A D-Class is sent into the SCP with a notebook, in which their experiences are recorded.

Hook/Attention Grabber:  The road is some sort of closed reality that extends on forever, forward and backward; the twist, though, is that there's actually no more to the road than can be seen from observing it - it's not really an infinite road, but one section of a road repeating infinitely.

Additional Notes:  Any feedback is appreciated. Is this too generic? I've written out a draft if anyone wants more info.





